{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And now, when I come to your servant my father and the lad is not with us.</b> Since he testified to us here that this will indeed be so, it will not be attributed to chance, but it will be fitting to attribute it to us — that we brought this harm about with our own hands, as in: פֶּן תֹּאמַר עָצְבִּי עָשָׂם (Isaiah 48:5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "The verse citation Isaiah 48:5 is given as ישעיהו מח:ה in the Hebrew; the full phrase quoted begins בְּטֶרֶם תָּבוֹא הִשְׁמַעְתִּיךָ but the verse reference points to the continuation including פֶּן תֹּאמַר עָצְבִּי עָשָׂם."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:37.510921406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}